            "Even after practicing well, then, we may still fail to control our mind or eliminate jealousy. As soon as someone appears to compete with our interests, jealousy arises. Could our fine teaching and service to sentient beings actually conceal private ambitions rather than sincere devotion to the Dharma and their welfare? If we truly loved sentient beings, we would rejoice to hear of another good teacher. Instead, we fear losing prestige, influence, and benefits. That is jealousy. We must be careful. If sentient beings benefit, we must rejoice, whoever guides them."
